          "title": "You'll want to know: कृपया तूष्णीं भव",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कृपया तूष्णीं भव। kṛpayā tūṣṇīṃ bhava. “Please be quiet.”"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Board of School Education Haryana copy of the NCERT Class 10 Śemuṣī Sanskrit reader uses the exact command तूष्णीं भव. The grammatical commentary on Pāṇini 3.4.63 also explicitly treats तूष्णीम् with √भू. The कृपया at the front is the “please” you already know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: one complete request",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This lesson owns the complete familiar-person request. It does not teach the imperative paradigm, and it does not license you to manufacture other command forms from भव."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
